open-skyfall and uses Intgral's brand mark. The upstream SolidCraft copyright and
licence notices above remain in force for the upstream code and assets.

Third-party material

Software dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock; their licences are in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt
(`cargo xtask licences`), which the programs also carry (Help > About > Licences,
`solidcraft-cli licences`). The geometry kernel builds on the truck crates
(truck-modeling, truck-shapeops, truck-meshalgo, truck-stepio, truck-topology and their
dependencies, https://github.com/ricosjp/truck), licensed under the Apache License 2.0 and used
as libraries. truck-shapeops 0.4.0 is vendored in vendor/truck-shapeops with SolidCraft
modifications (listed in vendor/README.md and marked in the source); its licence is in
vendor/truck-shapeops/LICENSE. Copyright (c) RICOS Co. Ltd.

Desktop web view. The Assistant's interface on Linux is drawn by the system's GTK 3 and
WebKitGTK 4.1 libraries: the app loads them as unmodified shared libraries through the
wry, gtk and webkit2gtk Rust crates. GTK 3 is LGPL-2.1-or-later; WebKitGTK is LGPL and
BSD-2-Clause. Neither library is copied, modified or bundled by the deb, rpm, tarball or
AppImage; the Nix package's closure does carry both. Copyright notices, licence texts and
what each package must ship are in docs/web-view-licences.md and
packaging/notices/WEB-VIEW-PLATFORM-NOTICES.txt. On Windows the Assistant uses the
Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime, which the MSI and portable build do not redistribute; the
WebView2Loader static library compiled into the executable comes from Microsoft's WebView2
SDK and is subject to Microsoft's terms. On macOS the Assistant uses the system's WKWebView
framework. These are notices, not a legal clearance.

Some code is adapted from sibling projects in the storytold family (CADCraft, GridCraft), which are
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; ATTRIBUTION.md lists the files.
The release packaging (.github/workflows/release.yml, packaging/) is adapted from PhotoCraft
(https://github.com/storytold/photocraft), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

The incremental Radiance RGBE row adapter in crates/render/src/lighting/hdr.rs adapts
decoding state machines from image 0.25.10 (https://github.com/image-rs/image),
MIT OR Apache-2.0. ATTRIBUTION.md describes the bounded/cancellable changes; the
original licence texts are included in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.

Most bundled assets are drawn in code or contributed originally; third-party fonts (Liberation Sans
for sketch text, BIZ UDPGothic for web Japanese display) are licensed under SIL OFL 1.1. The
per-file list is in ATTRIBUTION.md.

